        "id": 23830,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-06-27T09:15:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree with McBehrer.   I mean…   I don’t know,   Wraith is already a very powerful hero, so on one hand the thought of giving her a buff is kind of bad.   But OTOH it seems just silly for her combat stance to include occasionally whacking her allies in the face.     This is especially the case with Embolden and Combat Stance or Flame Barrier, and it really hurts the effectiveness of all 3 of these cards.</p>\n<p>You could of course just word it so it only takes effect when the hero was dealt damage by a villain/environment card.    I feel that would be the more elegant solution.  That way you’d not be able to avoid dealing damage to villain cards that you didn’t want in the trash, so Combat Stance would become in some ways kind of like Electrical Storm.</p>",
