        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-24T03:12:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had this question tonight, and I see that it took a while to reach consensus.&nbsp; I'll go with the Christopher quote Broccoli posted, even though it's secondhand.</p>\n<p>As to the \"should you retaliate against your fellow heroes\" question, I think it'd be nice if the answer was \"yes\" for Ra and \"no\" for Wraith, as it would seem more fitting that way, for both flavor reasons (Ra is an imperious ancient god, Wraith is a friendly young lady) and mechanical ones (Combat Stance is Wraith choosing to punch someone, Flame Barrier is Ra being on fire).&nbsp; In general, I am always favor of making the heroes more individualized.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"mcbehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> mcbehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>On the other hand, Wraith being infected, hitting herself, and then retaliating against herself is just plain stupid. And I mean wallbanger territory.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I dunno, I got the Chairman to retaliate against himself once and it was pretty frickin' hilarious.&nbsp; I figure that if Wraith is deadly in hand-to-hand combat, then an Infection making her deadly even to herself sort of fits.&nbsp; Figure that she's berserking and attacking imaginary enemies and periodically bashing her face into a wall or something.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:57:49.706Z",
