      {
        "id": 23844,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-24T09:05:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Either way, it's fire, and thus it cannot choose to not burn things that step into it.&nbsp; Whereas Wraith could in theory choose not to punch people who get too close to her, although I can see the argument for saying she reacts on instinct before she has time to recognize friend (or even self) from foe.&nbsp; Even so, I can see no argument for saying the Flame Barrier shouldn't be 100% automatic, and like I said, I wish they were different just for the sake of being so.</p>",
